  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: Collections\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: Collections\n       Program: commons-collections\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Collections/Collections.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-collections.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Collections/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 28\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: Collections-9\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\n8a5d3acab88bb2ef7416f3141d63f10b79d318cf\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2008-03-16 01:39:13 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nCOLLECTIONS-271\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/COLLECTIONS-271\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.collections.TestExtendedProperties::testCollections271\n   --> junit.framework.AssertionFailedError: expected:<\\\\192.168.1.91\\test> but was:<\\192.168.1.91\\test>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.collections.ExtendedProperties\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: org.apache.commons.collections.ExtendedProperties#combine don't import string properly\nType: Bug | Priority: Major | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nWhen we set property with escaped characters, after combine propertySets we got them unescaped.\n\nSimple Example\n\nExtendedProperties props = new ExtendedProperties();\nprops.setProperty(\"test\", \"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\192.168.1.91\\\\\\\\test\");\nprops.getProperty(\"test\"); // => \\\\192.168.1.91\\test\n\nExtendedProperties props2 = new ExtendedProperties();\nprops2.combine(props);\nprops.getProperty(\"test\"); // => \\192.168.1.91\\test -- Wrong!\n\nComments:\n\n[Alexander Borovsky]: Possible fix attached\n\n[Henri Yandell]: Bug confirmed - but the fix doesn't pass the unit test so might need something more.\n\n[Henri Yandell]: Unit test and fix attached. Needed to make it super.put and not put in the fix.\n\n[Henri Yandell]: svn ci -m \"Applying the patch from Alexander Borovsky for COLLECTIONS-271\" src\nSending        src/java/org/apache/commons/collections/ExtendedProperties.java\nSending        src/test/org/apache/commons/collections/TestExtendedProperties.java\nTransmitting file data ..\nCommitted revision 637503.\n\n[Nathan Bubna]: I think your patch for this breaks getKeys() after a combine() call.  It appears to make combine() not track new keys, which breaks both getKeys() and subset().  Because combine() then subset() is broken, Velocity has been experiencing frustratingly mysterious failures for months now.  For more on the symptoms, see:\n\nhttp://tinyurl.com/5hjxrq\n\nI suspect instead of super.put(), the patch for this should have used clearProperty() followed by addPropertyDirect().  Of course, i haven't tested that...",
